ExxonMobil’s most recent MD&A (10-Q for Q1 FY2026, Accession 0000034088-26-000093) identifies a number of climate-related and regulatory risks that could affect its business and results.  In particular, the company calls out:  

1. Government policies and taxes aimed at lower-carbon energy, including punitive European taxes on oil & gas, and uneven support for different emissions-reduction technologies;  
2. Evolving, ambiguous and unharmonized voluntary or mandatory standards or extraterritorial laws and regulations related to sustainability and greenhouse-gas reporting;  
3. Timely granting of permits, licenses and certifications (e.g. for new projects or facilities);  
4. Uncertain impacts of deregulation on the legal and regulatory environment;  
5. Development and competitiveness of alternative energy and emissions-reduction technologies; and  
6. Consumer preferences, including willingness and ability to pay for reduced-emission products.  

